---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Programs
description: "Infant, toddler, preschool and school age programs at Precious Steps in Plainfield, NJ, with age ranges, teacher to child ratios and curricula."
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Programs</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">A classroom for every stage</h1>
    <p class="hero__lead">
      We use the High Scope curriculum with our infants, toddlers and Room to
      Bloom children, and Connect 4 Learning in our district Pre-K classrooms.
      Both are built around active, hands-on learning.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{% for program in programs %}
  <section class="section{% if loop.index0 % 2 == 1 %} section--subtle{% endif %}" id="{{ program.id }}">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <h2>{{ program.name }}</h2>

      <dl class="spec">
        <dt>Ages</dt>
        <dd>{{ program.ages }}</dd>
        <dt>Teacher to child ratio</dt>
        <dd>{{ program.ratio }}</dd>
        <dt>Curriculum</dt>
        <dd>{{ program.curriculum }}</dd>
      </dl>

      {% if not program.agesConfirmed %}
        <div class="todo">
          <strong>Unconfirmed age range</strong>
          {{ program.agesNote }}
        </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if program.summary %}
        <p>{{ program.summary }}</p>
      {% else %}
        <div class="todo">
          <strong>Content needed</strong>
          {{ program.sourceNote }}
        </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if program.schedule %}
        <h3>A typical day</h3>
        <p>{{ program.schedule }}</p>
      {% endif %}

      {% if program.bring.length %}
        <h3>What to bring</h3>
        <ul>
          {% for item in program.bring %}
            <li>{{ item }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
{% endfor %}

<section class="section section--ruled">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <h2>Meals</h2>
    <p>
      Meals and snacks are provided under the New Jersey Child and Adult Care
      Food Program and meet USDA nutritional standards. Menus are posted
      monthly. We practice family style dining, where children and staff eat
      together at the table and children serve themselves from appropriately
      sized bowls and pitchers.
    </p>
    <p>
      We accommodate food allergies as directed by your child's physician.
      Precious Steps is a nut free center.
    </p>

    <h2>Field trips</h2>
    <p>
      We provide transportation for field trips. Parents sign a blanket
      permission slip at registration for walks and visits in the community, and
      a trip-specific permission slip for any outing requiring transportation
      away from the center.
    </p>

    <h2>Staying in touch</h2>
    <p>
      We use Brightwheel as our primary communication platform, with ClassDojo
      also in use. Meals, diaper changes and daily activities are posted by
      teachers each day, and parent teacher conferences are held three times a
      year.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

